### 3. Backend: The Service Layer (The API Logic)
**File:** The Service class that fetches the pending list (e.g., VoucherQueryService.java or VoucherWorkflowService.java).
This is where you calculate the time and attach it to the DTO before sending it to the frontend.
```java
import java.time.Duration;
import java.time.LocalDateTime;
import java.util.Optional;

// ... inside your service class ...

@Autowired
private VoucherWorkflowRepository workflowRepository;

// 1. Add this private helper method to do the math
private String calculateTimeSinceLastAction(String batchId) {
    Optional<VoucherWorkflow> latestAction = 
        workflowRepository.findTopByBatchIdFkOrderByLastActionAtDesc(batchId);

    if (latestAction.isEmpty() || latestAction.get().getLastActionAt() == null) {
        return "0h 0m";
    }

    Duration duration = Duration.between(latestAction.get().getLastActionAt(), LocalDateTime.now());
    return duration.toHours() + "h " + duration.toMinutesPart() + "m";
}

